{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787548151372021001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"synonymous-senatorial-cuscus","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"fdb46575f2c66688ab1e405d58e1839639d26e4c80623e31e763e4562b68548d","event_uuid":"836b482b-8846-4799-890c-fa1c5f746c9d","position":{"commit_sha":"425afc0d2297b77c938da664abb94e4c7f02094c","position":"1787544215405453001-836b482b-8846-4799-890c-fa1c5f746c9d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"12e51d04927c189256bc61bed9e6dbce30d7176b3f076464de6a11952e2074ec","event_uuid":"02da6e80-6ed0-4d07-8fd0-b21062bfb1e8","position":{"commit_sha":"f65076c4bee78cd927570bb8dc7ad76eb69932f2","position":"1787544284167455001-02da6e80-6ed0-4d07-8fd0-b21062bfb1e8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"8f474a2c180aacee122621cea16dbe20e0ab31c3fd802dcbd527b940bea8dbfc","event_uuid":"70e54c20-2f91-4516-a0dc-866a8ad34d3c","position":{"commit_sha":"db87d6bce9d588b8f69405c3e4aaf4432ecb44e1","position":"1787544390091741001-70e54c20-2f91-4516-a0dc-866a8ad34d3c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787544215405453001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"02da6e80-6ed0-4d07-8fd0-b21062bfb1e8","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"93c4-2b9f-749a-4243"}],"description":"## Context\n\nPreparation ticket irongray-unlucky-discus builds and validates the manifest-driven local rewrite package for the six proven reconciler echo groups. This ticket owns the destructive production quiet window only.\n\nDO NOT CLAIM OR START this ticket until:\n- irongray-unlucky-discus is merged and closed;\n- its real-store read-only rehearsal and rollback/stale-writer proofs pass;\n- the operator explicitly says the quiet window may begin;\n- this execution plan has a current signed plan-review attestation.\n\nThe present user approval covers preparation, not activation. No fixed waiting period can substitute for direct writer/runtime evidence.\n\n## Authorized semantic delta\n\nAt the frozen tickets tip, remove only the non-survivor COMMENT events enumerated by the signed immutable manifest and the same entries embedded in enumerated active/retired snapshots. Retain one live-Jira-identity local echo per each of the six groups. Preserve every bridge comment_ids key and real mapped id, every non-candidate event byte/signature, every unrelated ticket state, and every non-target snapshot field. Add only the new store epoch required to reject stale clones.\n\nIf live Jira has zero or multiple matching copies, pagination is incomplete, the map conflicts with the live id, target counts/body hashes drift, or any non-target parity check fails, abort without publication. Jira deletion is outside this ticket unless separately and explicitly approved.\n\n## Quiet-window protocol\n\n1. Confirm the deployed comment-id and marker repairs by direct ancestry/runtime evidence and two unchanged production-equivalent reconcile observations with no new target-body events; record exact runs and tips.\n2. Pause every writer: reconcile/canary workflows and redispatch, review-bot voting after in-flight/pending work drains, MCP servers, active agent sessions, host updaters/GC, and scheduled/autodeploy writers. Record exact runtime identities and direct zero-in-flight proofs. Do not use a fixed sleep.\n3. Freeze the exact remote tickets tip/lease and complete live Jira inventories. Generate and review the immutable target manifest. Refuse any tip or inventory movement.\n4. From a fresh unfiltered non-promisor clone, create the complete off-repo bundle and manifest, independently restore every bundled ref, and prove the rollback command against a throwaway remote before any publication.\n5. Produce the local candidate and run all gates: exact path/blob delta, graph/merge counts, full replay state oracle, retained authorship parity, fsck, bridge-map byte parity, six live survivor identities, new epoch, old-tip non-ancestry, and all footprint layers.\n6. Publish only through the reviewed audited reclaim surface with an exact old-tip force-with-lease. No ad-hoc raw Git and no force option lacking the exact expected OID.\n7. Re-clone or hard-converge every persistent writer from the new epoch, carrying the four ignored identity files where required. Prove stale pre-epoch clones refuse both sync-union and push-recovery union without merging.\n8. Observe the first post-window write, prove the old tip was not resurrected by any default-fetched ref, then restore writers in recorded order. Require two unchanged reconciler passes with no replacement target comments.\n9. Run final fsck, retained-authorship, semantic parity, and tracker-footprint observations. Notify the operator that sessions may resume.\n10. Rollback, if required, is a second quiesced window: restore the independently verified bundle with an exact current-tip lease, re-converge all persistent writers, and repeat post-read verification. Never bypass the epoch guard.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] [operator-attested] Every writer is directly proven quiescent and every deployed runtime identity/ancestry is recorded before the lease is frozen.\n      provenance: environment=production writer fleet; principal=operator and RebarBotNava; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — workflow, health, process, session, and runtime ancestry receipts are recorded on this ticket.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] Complete Jira inventories and the frozen store produce one signed immutable manifest with exactly one live identity-backed survivor per group and no ambiguity.\n      provenance: environment=Jira Cloud production plus fresh tickets clone; principal=RebarBotNava; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — paginated totals, ids, hashes, source tip, and manifest digest are recorded before publication.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] A complete off-repo bundle is independently restored and exact rollback succeeds against a throwaway remote before publication.\n      provenance: environment=isolated local restore rehearsal; principal=RebarBotNava; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=CLI subprocess — bundle heads, restore OIDs, and lease results are recorded.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] Pre-publication parity proves the only state delta is the manifest echo set plus epoch; fsck, retained authorship, graph shape, bridge-map, and survivor checks pass.\n      provenance: environment=fresh unfiltered production-history clone; principal=RebarBotNava; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=CLI subprocess — machine-readable verifier artifacts and hashes are recorded.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] The exact old-tip lease advances tickets once; no default-fetched ref retains old ancestry; persistent writers are re-cloned/converged; synthetic and live stale writers refuse without merge.\n      provenance: environment=origin tickets plus persistent writer clones; principal=operator and RebarBotNava; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — ref snapshots, lease OIDs, clone epochs, and refusal receipts are recorded.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] Two unchanged post-enable reconcile passes create no target comments or map divergence, final fsck/parity pass, and all footprint layers are reported as observations without thresholds.\n      provenance: environment=production reconciler and fresh tickets clone; principal=RebarBotNava; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — run ids, event deltas, verifier outputs, and footprint JSON are recorded.\n- [ ] The operator is notified before the quiet window begins and again before sessions may resume.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"none","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","93c4-2b9f-749a-4243"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"Production operation only: it uses the separately landed reclaim package and changes the tickets ref, not code-repository files.","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["store","reconciler","reclaim","quiet-window"],"ticket_id":"6e2f-2814-4f92-4873","ticket_type":"task","title":"Execute the targeted comment-echo history reclaim quiet window","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["836b482b-8846-4799-890c-fa1c5f746c9d","02da6e80-6ed0-4d07-8fd0-b21062bfb1e8","70e54c20-2f91-4516-a0dc-866a8ad34d3c"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787548151372021001,"uuid":"a2fe907f-efe2-4dc0-8fbd-fc6752a827a5"}